# -*- mode:org; coding:utf-8 -*-
#+TITLE: verify:epure:windows's EPURE API rows call functions EPURE does not load, and pass on failure
#+STATUS: TODO
#+PRIORITY: P3
#+TYPE: bug
#+DEPENDS: -
#+BRANCH: fix-verify-epure-api-rows
#+DATE: 2026-11-19

* Symptom

scripts/verify-epure-windows.ps1 runs, per CAD, two forms through
alfe --epure, once with -x and once from a file:

: (print (= "" (toutes_options nil)))
: (print (equal (quote ((enabled) (message))) (f_DateHeure_UTC 0)))

On PF5S26BT all four rows fail, the same on 2026-11-17 (job 18100605445,
EPURE on V:) and 2026-11-19 (job 18182663143, EPURE on the local copy):

- from the file: exit 1, "no function definition: TOUTES_OPTIONS";
- with -x: exit 75 after "CAD did not acknowledge session restoration
  before shutdown. [RESTORE-NOT-ACKNOWLEDGED]" (AutoCAD), exit 69 (BricsCAD,
  2026-11-17).

Yet the job succeeds: its gate counts only a row that exits 0 without its
marker.

* Three things

1. The forms test functions EPURE does not load at start-up: toutes_options
   is in COM/gestsauv/Sauvprm.lsp (see the notes in
   scripts/verify-epure-api.ps1, which tests com_way / com_tl_continu
   instead and passes). Replace them, or drop the rows.
2. The gate lets a nonzero exit through: a timeout (75) or an error (1) on
   an EPURE row must fail the job.
3. The same undefined-function error gives exit 1 from a file but exit 75
   with RESTORE-NOT-ACKNOWLEDGED from -x: alfe's -x error path does not
   reach the restoration handshake. To reproduce off Windows with a
   plugin-less --autocad / --bricscad -x on an undefined function, if the
   file-protocol backend shows it too.
